WEBVTT

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.690
Saegusa, do you hear me?

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.940
Come on out of there, Mirei!

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.110
Stop this nonsense!

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.940
Saegusa, answer us!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:18.450
If only... If only it weren't
for this leg... If only...

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.250
Saegusa! Do you realize
what you are about to do?!

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.620
Please, Mirei, open this door!

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.500
Stay away! I can't take any more!
I'll never skate again!

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.170
From now on, I'm living the way<i> I </i>want to!

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.050
Don't make any hasty decisions!

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.100
I'm breaking it down!

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.070
Farewell to who I've been up to today.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.070
Whoa...

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:30.060
<i>ENTER THE RED DOORS</i>

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:50.670
<i>Up above the forest of slumber</i>

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:57.340
<i>Two moons look down from the sky</i>

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:04.850
<i>Where did you come from,</i>
<i>and where are you going?</i>

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:13.230
<i>Where are we going?</i>

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:18.860
<i>ENTER THE RED DOORS</i>

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.420
Hmm. So that dream
would have to be a witch.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:38.010
Probably. Even I can tell that much.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.340
What are you so angry about?

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.230
I don't like seeing people in pain.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.760
Mirei Saegusa... I've heard of her.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.350
Really, who breaks their own
leg with a hatchet?

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.020
It must have been a pretty big deal.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.520
A cute girl like her...

00:02:58.900 --> 00:02:59.990
Are you in love?

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.030
It's not <i>that</i>!

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:05.830
All right. We know her name.
I'll do some checking on my end.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:09.880
Once I access the database, I ought to
be able to find something to go on.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.630
But listen to me;
I'm going to say this plainly--

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.500
She's a witch. Your love 
isn't going anywhere.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.340
I told you, it's not like that!

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.850
Huh? For me, too?

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.470
If you don't want it, fine.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.230
Mirei Saegusa, 18, figure skater.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.580
At age three, her grandfather
took her to a local ice rink,

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.250
where she discovers skating.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.200
She picks up spins and 
jumps by watching others,

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.330
and is scouted out by a skating school
coach while she's skating for fun.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.340
She becomes a household name

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.020
by winning the All-Japan
Championship at the age of 14.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.090
She becomes a domestic superstar.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.050
Afterward, with her rich
expressiveness and technical skill,

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:02.680
she takes the world by storm, and,
coupled with her endearing good looks,

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.800
--becomes a national idol.
--Mirei Cocoa is the flavor of love.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.180
"High-Flying Jumper"

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.550
As the favorite in the upcoming Olympics...

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.550
"Fairy on Ice"

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.930
"Goddess of the Rink"

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.310
...she enjoys the fame of being a phenomenon.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.310
"World's Greatest"

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.890
In her last appearance,
at the world championships,

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.190
she messed up a triple jump and fell,
ending up in second place.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.730
Immediately afterward, 
for unexplained reasons,

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:21.280
she came down with Sleeping Beauty
Syndrome, and fell into a coma.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.780
So now what?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.540
Saegusa, do you hear me?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.210
Come on out of there, Mirei!

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:40.050
Stay away! I can't take any more!
I'll never skate again!

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.700
From now on, I'm living the way<i> I</i> want to!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.680
Farewell to who I've been up to today.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:50.510
You like her?

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.390
W-What? When did you get here?

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.230
Mirei <i>is</i> pretty, isn't she?

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:56.730
Huh?

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.550
You look like you're wondering how I know.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.240
I can tell. I know everything
about you, Brother.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.200
Again, what is it with this "Brother"--

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.240
I think she's crying for help.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.070
Huh?

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.080
Maybe she's sending a telepathic message.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.280
Gotcha!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.080
Huh?

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.090
I'm kidding. I just wanted
to see what you'd do.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.340
Why, you... Mess with 
your brother, will you?!

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:26.220
There, you see? I've got 
you saying "Brother."

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.130
I never said that!

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.350
Did, too, did, too!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.350
"Ms. Mirei Saegusa"

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.960
Please excuse me.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:44.660
Yurina, don't you end up like this, too.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.820
Was she really that famous?

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.230
How is it I don't know her?

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.830
I suppose I don't watch
figure skating. Did you know?

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.330
Well, yeah.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:00.540
Still, why would a big star
like her smash her leg?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.130
In her last competition before
she went to sleep, she slipped up.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.340
She must have been driven
to despair over losing.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.640
If it were me, I'd never 
do anything like that.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.530
I'd have far too much fun being fussed over.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.720
There are worlds that the
common man can't understand.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:17.080
Maybe that's what it was.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:24.740
Say, what if we skipped
taking care of this witch?

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:26.860
Hm? What's this, all of sudden?

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:30.110
Oh, uh, this one is just...

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.870
You don't care about your sister?

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.160
Yes, I do, but...

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.540
I want to help this girl out.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:38.970
Huh?

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.370
Besides,

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.200
she's already here.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.190
If you're not up for it,
that's fine. I'll go by myself.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.390
Hold on. Why are you so gung-ho this time?

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.510
She came just to share her dream with me.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.350
I think it's some kind of sign.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:00.350
If I can do something for her,
I'd like to do it. Not to mention...

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.190
I can't walk away from a cute girl's
telepathic message, you know?

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:15.480
Well, I guess I have no right
to stop him, do I?

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:27.920
What do you know?
It's just a regular college.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.200
I-I'm so sorry!

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.990
Oh, no, my fault.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:43.230
Okay then, what do I do now?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:47.330
Figure skating? Do we even
have that at our college?

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.240
Mirei Saegusa? No, don't know her.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.660
If there were a cute girl like that here,
this place would be jumping.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.910
Give me 20,000, and I'll find her for--

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.990
Um, I can't seem to find her.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.920
Come on, use your head a little.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.690
Mirei Saegusa, someone from
your family is waiting for you.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.930
Please come to the General
Affairs windows at once.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.850
Excuse me, I'm Saegusa. 
I was just paged here.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.050
You said a family member was here...?

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.850
Wait, really? Didn't we just...?

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:31.110
Wow, I'm so glad I found you.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.010
But you have a whole
different image now, huh?

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.870
Excuse me, but have we met somewhere before?

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:41.870
Oh, we haven't met in person.
I mean, you're a celebrity, right?

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.350
Ah, hold on! Hold on a second!

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.050
I'm not going back! And who <i>are</i> you, anyway?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.970
What do you want, barging
into my world like this?!

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.550
You're the one who called <i>me</i>, aren't you?

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:56.140
Huh?

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.100
You came to me for help, right?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.850
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:03.680
I'm enjoying my life here.
Why would I want help?

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:04.780
Let me go.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:08.060
You enjoy it here?

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:11.110
Mind your own business.
This has nothing to do with you.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.190
It's just a regular college, isn't it?

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.200
I suppose you wouldn't understand, would you?

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.120
No, no one would understand.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.760
But I've made up my mind.
I'm going to live a different life.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.980
I'd been standing in the rink
for as long as I can remember.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.090
Every morning at five o'clock,
I went running for ten kilometers.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.680
After school, I skated at 
the rink until it closed,

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.840
and when I got back, it was gym work
and stretching until bedtime.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.390
Forget about field days 
and culture festivals,

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.220
it didn't even matter if I had a test.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:47.080
I didn't even get to go on
field trips or school excursions.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:49.520
I always ate meals in a moving vehicle,

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.060
and on days off, I spent 
20 hours in the rink.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:56.820
Have you ever been so exhausted
that you fell asleep on the ice?

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:08.990
Must be nice.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.960
Still, you started figure skating
because you liked it, right?

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.090
I still like it, even now.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:00.740
Then...

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.580
I've never thought that
my practices were too hard.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.640
But then, it isn't that I wanted a gold medal.
Nor did I want to be a star.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:10.420
I just...

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.690
I just want to live a normal life.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.190
A normal life?

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:21.090
When I was a child, I 
was happy just to skate.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.490
I wasn't anxious about anything.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.700
As long as I was on the 
ice, I could be myself.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:30.710
Then, at some point, I was besieged
by grownups I didn't know,

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.710
and before I knew it, I'd been made an idol.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:36.060
I didn't want any of that.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.720
When I realized what had happened,
I'd lost sight of myself.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.510
It's not as though I don't
get what you're saying,

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.520
but you're not missing anything.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:48.020
I mean, I don't think
a normal life is all that great.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.140
--If I had all your talent--

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.420
--I've had it!
--If I had all your talent--

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.100
I want to enjoy my youth
along with everyone else, too!

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:57.730
I want to experience what so many
other people experience for myself!

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:00.240
What's so wrong with wanting that?!

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.670
Going to school, studying,
playing with friends...

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.740
...finding lots of love...

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:13.560
Being able to enjoy this moment...
just like everyone else--

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.750
that's all I want, and yet...

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.700
You're right. I'm sorry.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:27.530
You <i>do</i> have the right 
to choose your own life.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:32.270
In that case, why don't you let me
show you an average campus life?

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:35.770
Who, you?

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:40.150
I <i>am</i>, after all, a college 
student, too. Come on.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:44.410
'Kay...

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.470
<i>18if</i>.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.500
So? How do you like
an average campus life?

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:46.430
It's incredibly fun! Coming here
was the correct decision, all right.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.600
Oh, yeah? Well if you're that delighted,

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.530
it was worth it giving you the tour.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.270
Let me guess--Yuki?

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:00.730
Wha--?!

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:05.440
Nice going! I'm behind you all
the way, really. I hope it goes well.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.690
Yeah, thanks.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.040
Saegusa!

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:20.540
Hey.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.750
Yuki!

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.510
Listen, are you free on Saturday?

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:28.090
Huh? Oh, yes. I have nothing special planned.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:31.760
In that case, I have two tickets
to a movie premiere.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:32.640
Want to come with me?

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.510
W-With you?!

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:36.390
What, am I not good enough?

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.520
N-No, nothing like that!

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.520
Okay, it's settled. This Saturday, okay?

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:42.970
I'll be in touch.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:44.570
Okay.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:49.110
What do I do, Haruto? I don't know
what I'm supposed to wear!

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.120
Anything you wear will be fine.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.620
You're used to performing
at major venues, right?

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:57.540
--Oh, jeez, what am I going to do?!
--Come on, give me a little advice
on the male mind that I can use!

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.620
"Yuki"

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.000
Oh, well, I don't know
if I can help you there.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.920
Look, can you come along the day of the date?

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.130
Don't be silly!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.240
Sorry to keep you.

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:11.980
H-Hello!

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.350
Waiting long?

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.010
No, not at all.

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.140
Wow, I almost didn't recognize you.

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:17.770
Huh?

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.890
Nothing. Well, ready to go?

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.900
Oh, yes.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:30.020
I got worried about her and came after all.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:09.710
I had no idea there was
such a pretty place nearby!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.490
You never came here as a kid?
Like on a school outing?

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:25.830
Listen, Yuki, thank you so much
for everything today.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.550
I've never experienced
anything like this before,

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.880
so it almost seems like I'm still dreaming.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:34.130
Oh, come on. All we did is
see a movie and get some tea.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.220
Yes, but, um...

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:39.710
I was very pleased we did it.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.630
Say, Saegusa, do you still have some time?

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:54.080
Huh?

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:57.980
There's one more place 
I'd like to go with you.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:16:59.990
But, um...

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.290
I'd like...

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.440
I'd like to get to know you a little better.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:07.990
Okay.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:18.800
Why...?

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.410
What's the matter?
You've never skated before?

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.640
No, I wouldn't say that.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.150
Good. Well, let's skate.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:30.170
S-Sure.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.190
Yeah.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.280
This is better.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.430
Ah, this sensation--

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.990
Um... I...

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:17.450
That was pretty. The prettiest
I've seen you so far.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.450
Yuki...

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.190
Yuki?!

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.350
Come back to us, Mirei!

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:43.720
Skate again!

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:46.600
Skate, Saegusa!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.020
Saegusa!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:53.940
Mirei! Mirei! Mirei! Mirei! Mirei!

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:56.560
Come on, skate, Mirei.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:00.450
After all, <i>this</i> is where you belong.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.880
N-No... Stop this...

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:09.210
No!

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:17.800
Like I told you, it isn't all that great.

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:24.260
But why? How did this happen?
This is my dream, isn't it?

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:28.020
I don't know. It was going
so well for a while there.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:32.400
But maybe that's just what your destiny is.

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.630
Des... tiny...?

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:39.420
The one place where you
can really be yourself is...

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:45.160
Yes. Ultimately, this is the
only path I have, isn't it?

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.810
That's right, Mirei.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:56.050
You shine brightest when you're on the ice.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:20:01.010
So keep right on skating. That's what your...

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:02.580
...destiny is.

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:09.960
Well, I'll be going, then.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:14.030
Let me see you skate sometime
in the outside world.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:34.880
It's all right. Knowing you,
you'll be able to overcome this.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:43.830
Mirei?

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.810
Can you understand me, Mirei Saegusa?!

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:50.020
Doctor! Doctor!

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:11.250
Did she seem happy?

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.210
Yeah. It looked like she had gotten over it.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.420
I see.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.130
Also...

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:19.940
I sensed something while looking at her.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.010
That there was something inescapable

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.600
that<i> I </i>have been carrying
without even realizing it.

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:28.930
What would that be?

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:29.710
Search me.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.900
Huh? Again?

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.300
If you don't want it, fine.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.730
No, I think I'll eat.

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:55.000
"The Witch of Ordinariness"

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.550
I'm looking forward to some skating.

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:30.260
If you became a hero of justice,

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:33.240
then you'd want to beat up
the bad guys, right?

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:35.450
Bad guys, baa!

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:41.540
"Curses Return Upon the Casters"

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:39.600
Next time's dream is
"Curses Return Upon the Casters."
